def line(s=''):out.append(s)
line('# ACR-06 C2b: 600-DPI sharing funnel (research only)')
line('')
line('Recommendation: **revise the investigation**. No bounded, physically justified change with demonstrated meaningful gain was identified, and no relaxed candidate was implemented. This does not establish that no useful safe gain is possible. In particular, the 1.5-source-pixel halo remains an unresolved scale-dependent question, not a demonstrated safe correction. The q3 and default decisions are unchanged. No holdout was opened and no Phase 3 candidate qualification is claimed.')
line('')
line('## Design and limits')
line('Development fixture: 18 identical text lines, same layout in points, five DejaVu faces and multiple sizes, seed 270602, rendered separately at 300 and 600 DPI. Generator, font and input hashes and the Bitstream Vera/DejaVu licence location are in `development-manifest.json`; PNGs and PDFs are in `local/c2b/development`. PIL integer font-size rounding and rasterization change the samples, as expected. These are clean repeated-font pages with little independent design variation and are not representative holdouts. OCR produces 273 emitted occurrences in both pages but different eligible cohorts. Spent sheets are P2/P2prime/P2pp 6–8 and FONT-01 train/validation/test 2, 600 DPI. This worktree is based on main 9655fcc; numbers need not reproduce the older 79b30e5 study exactly.')
line('')
line('`SCANWEAVE_RESEARCH_C2B_TRACE=<path>` writes occurrences, eligible rows, all tested fits, cover groups, and final pre-economy decisions to that path; ownership outcomes are in `<path>.ownership.json`. Null ownership outcomes mean invalid geometry and remain vetoes. The ordinary q3 sidecar supplies economy and final decisions. Trace artifacts are large and live in `local/c2b/trace`. `run.py` pins PDFium and thread limits. `summarize.py` replays the deterministic cover, checks the replay against actual groups, and computes member-existence counts. The existence columns are successive filters over a member’s tested non-self pairs; they are not a disjoint accounting of causal failure, and no claim is made about untested pairs beyond the 24 nearest candidates. Cover columns partition eligible members, with selected groups listed before ownership. Cross-stage differences can include canonical selection and greedy cover interactions.')
line('')
line('## Funnel')
line('')
line('| document | occurrences | cohort ≥10 | frame / trace | any structural fit | + hygiene / band | + relative ≤2 | + absolute ≤0.08 | self-admissible | cover below quorum | no self candidate left | planned |')
line('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
for n,v in d.items():
 c=v['counts'];g=lambda k:c.get(k,0)
 line(f"| {n} | {g('occurrences')} | {g('eligible_label_at_least_10')} | {g('frame')} / {g('canonical_trace')} | {g('any_structural_pass')} | {g('any_hygiene_band_pass')} | {g('any_relative_pass')} | {g('any_absolute_pass')} | {g('self_admissible_canonical')} | {g('cover_below_quorum_members')} | {g('cover_no_self_admissible_remaining')} | {g('planned_members')} |")
line('')
line('| document | planned | legacy invalid | legacy true | corrected true | corrected invalid | combined veto | survive final quorum before economy | emitted | fallback |')
line('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|')
for n,v in d.items():
 c=v['counts'];e=v['economy'];g=lambda k:c.get(k,0)
 line(f"| {n} | {g('planned_members')} | {g('legacy_invalid')} | {g('legacy_reject')} | {g('corrected_reject')} | {g('corrected_invalid')} | {g('combined_reject')} | {g('final_accepted_before_economy')} | {e['substituted']} | {e['fallback'] or '—'} |")
line('')
line('The 12 spent 600-DPI sheets have 4,233 eligible members, 1,908 with at least one structurally passing non-self fit, 1,450 after hygiene/band, 1,418 after the relative ceiling, and 794 after the absolute ceiling. Greedy cover consumes 2,714 members in groups below its distinct-design quorum; 1,358 remain with no self-admissible canonical, and 161 enter planned groups. These cover categories partition the eligible members and are not interchangeable with the pair-existence counts. Of the 161 planned members, 88 encounter the combined ownership veto, leaving 33 members after final group checks; six members in FONT-01 train then fall back for document economy. Legacy invalid occurs 65 times and corrected true 38 times, with overlap. See the per-member trace for all outcomes.')
line('')
line('The matched development pages have 170 versus 167 eligible members, and 3 versus 9 planned members. At 600 DPI six planned members have invalid legacy geometry and all groups fail final quorum; at 300 DPI the three planned members survive. The fixture does not reproduce the large 300-DPI retirement rate of the spent corpus and does not isolate how much of that corpus gap comes from genuine detail versus sampling, OCR, or upstream grouping. The spent-sheet filter counts and the paired fixture point to an upstream bottleneck as well as the known veto; they do not provide a controlled causal estimate for each stage.')
line('')
line('## Scale and visual investigation')
line('The 2.0 relative and 0.08 absolute limits apply to mean squared coverage error on a 64×64 canvas scaled by line x-height, not a direct distance in source pixels. A raw multiplication of either ceiling by DPI is not physically justified. Registration translation bounds are also in this normalized canvas. The source preparation does use a fixed two-pixel grayscale halo and `dist <= 1.5` source pixels; it has a different physical extent at 600 DPI. Its purpose includes excluding nearby foreign ink and sampling antialiased edges, so physical rescaling alone is not proof of a defect or of safe improvement; the available halo would also need careful treatment. No counterfactual trial here establishes how much this quantity contributes to the gap.')
line('')
line('For a diagnostic only, `rejected_pairs.py` selects 12 P2 sheet 6 pairs whose best structural/hygiene/band/relative passing fit exceeds 0.08. The native source crops are `local/c2b/rejected-pairs.png` (SHA-256 `7d2dcdb01a8f9692db7849c608c604ed75b879b328a19c0c28832da5a8f0aac2`). The sample includes clear variations in serif, proportions and weight, and apparent same-label OCR mismatches. For example, `w000078s0003` versus `w000069s0000` has visibly different a designs, and `w000028s0007` versus `w000012s0007` appears to pair C and S under label s. OCR boxes can include neighbours and these are source crops, not isolated rendered substitutions; inspect them as diagnostic examples, not a population estimate. These differences make an across-the-board ceiling relaxation especially risky.')
line('')
line('Claude’s prior C2 review found 35 additional 600-DPI substitutions and only 7,423 bytes saved from corrected-only, with visible weight/proportion changes and individual pristine-error increases. The present run does not repeat that experiment or qualify those substitutions. No new substitutions exist in this work, so all-new-substitution panels, fidelity/ownership assessments, holdout, off/main/candidate economy, renderer diffs and candidate runtime comparison are inapplicable. The worrying examples above are rejected pairs, not newly admitted glyphs.')
line('')
